Z||000004||John Johnston||02-25-99||09:52 PM||||I also want to thank you for setting this up. I just bought a black 1987 Fiero GT about two weeks ago. I was also curious about installing some subwoofers. I have been told that the only things that would really work is "shakers", which could be mounted behind the seats but might cause abrasion on the seat backs. There isn't much room in a Fiero for speakers!
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||02-26-99||11:00 PM||||No, I didn't try putting subs in. I was trying to get info on Fiero stuff while deciding to buy one or not.. However, I was flamed so many times for just asking simple questions, I left the list and decided to wait to buy a Fiero until I can afford all the mods I want to do. ;) (twin turbo V8, Finale body kit, etc..)<p>I did however hear from some people who successfully put subs in a Fiero. One person I talked to said he got I think a pair of 8" Kicker subs behind the seats, and another person said they used the "bazooka tubes". I was personally thinking of using the Aura Bass Shakers in place of subs. they'd attach under the seat and to the firewall (4 in total) and should be pretty cool..
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||02-26-99||11:04 PM||||Another place I've seen a sub installed in a Fiero is in the front, in place of the spare tire. An excellent page that has photos of some extensive Fiero sound stuff is located at: http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/<br>but the page isn't done yet. I wanna see what they did with the stock door panels, the new console and dash were pretty cool.
Z||000007||iskydiveto||03-01-99||09:51 AM||||Subs in a Fiero? It's fun if you like a lot of hard work and standing on your head. I own JM Custom Autosound in Waupaca, WI and I have installed Subs in 2 Fieros. One was for a customer, I put an 8" JL Audio under the dash by the passenger seat. The other was my own car. I put a pair of Soundtream SPL 10's in the front (spare tire) compartment. This enclosure was fully sealed and make out of fiberglass and MDF. I then bandpassed it into the car with 2 ports, one by each footwell. It sounded great!<br>Remember, to achieve good bass, you only need to pressurize the space IN the car, so 10's were actually overkill.<br>The single 8" JL hit 132db on my meter, and the pair of Soundstreams hit a solid 143db.<br>Trust me, unless you want trashed eardrums and a lot of noise tickets, stick with the single 8.<br>Any questions, feel free to email me<br>Jim
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||03-03-99||04:13 PM||||any estimates as to how loud a ported JL 10" sub would be, mounted in the front compartment?
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||03-03-99||04:17 PM||||speaking of bass, last year I was working at a nuclear station as a co-op student, and one of the people I was working with is a stereo installer. That was what first got me interested in car audio. He had a 12" MTX in the back of his Mustang, and it was very loud. One of the coolest things about it tho, was how loud it was *outside* the car.. one time he was driving down main street, and a couple people started dancing.. quite funny!
Z||000010||iskydiveto||03-05-99||10:38 PM||||Hmm, one JL 10? Depends on the power pushing it, and these series of the sub(10w1,10w4,10w6?). 200watts rms mono into a 10W4 should hit about 130-135, but the enclosure and port design has to be PERFECT. I suggest you take it to a well knonw shop in your area, and be sure and check out some of their work before you let them hack your Fiero. This means actual customers cars, not just their own "money is no object" demo cars. Good Luck,<br>Jim
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||03-07-99||06:12 PM||||I'm not sure what the rating on the amp was,<br>but bridged it is 600 watts peak power.<br>the sub is a JL 10w6..<p>I'll ask the guy what the amp rating is, I<br>haven't bought it yet.
Z||000012||Psych0sis||03-16-99||02:13 AM||||Fiero's and subs..hmmm   Well My friend put 3 twelves in the trunk in a custom built encloser. (he actually used the trunk it self and lined it with 4 layers of dynamat.and then installed a face board for the subs)You wouldn't think it would sound good but guess what!?  you could here it 3 blocks away..the subs were Jl audio's and the amp was a ppi a600. That was how I discovered PPI equipment.he had to stagger the subs like this fit them in  .`.
Z||000013||inskip||04-09-99||10:20 PM||||Good evening fiero folks. I'm the new kid (sorta) on the block. i just purchase my frist Fiero. Its a '87 GT. I really enjoy it. I do have 2 Questions for you out there. 1) How can I start a Fiero club out here in the true northern calif. area and 2) my Fiero was built in Canada, and guess what, its all in kilo's and centameters and such. How do I convert the every to the american way of life??????? Thanks. Its great to have a group like this
